  "body": "For example, `ProgressEvent.lengthComputable`. This makes it sound like it's a static property of the `ProgressEvent` class.\n\nInstead, do \"`ProgressEvent`'s `lengthComputable` attribute\", or \"the `lengthComputable` attribute of `ProgressEvent`\". In example contexts, `progressEvent.lengthComputable` (i.e. lowercase to show it being an instance of the class) works as well.\n\nA sufficiently-clever regexp, run on the source, should be able to find these. There are several in the \"terms defined elsewhere\" section, but I imagine we use it throughout the spec sometimes as well.\n",
